From 0fefd36538859c4341c0694165fc5771af0b34fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 02:28:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09221/11362] Unblock .555 -- and the two violations needed
 OPPOSITE treatments

Second activation deadlock in three hours. Yesterday's note said the planner would
do this again; it did. But a blanket auto-override would have been wrong, because
the two HARD violations are not the same kind of thing.

exp6459-v555-adversarial-capstone -> operator_override. Routine milestone
transition, CLAUDE.md class 1. A capstone scope-matches every prior capstone by
construction and is structurally never a doomed rerun.

exp6454-held-exact-constraint-energy-selection-ab -> prior_failures, NOT an
override. This is a RESEARCH task, and the override class is for routine
transitions only. Using it here is precisely the abuse its own guardrail warns
about -- and the scope it matches is the energy-selection lineage that
project_energy_selection_thesis_bounded records as settled-negative, so it is
exactly the case where waving it through would be worst.

Read the four matched priors before deciding rather than pattern-matching the
name:

  exp1006  blocked_gate_check_failed     never executed a comparison
  exp5708  blocked: parse_failures       blocked on parsing, not on selection
  exp6205  blocked_gate_check_failed     never ran, blocked on upstream readiness
  exp787   energy_prefilter_efficient    ran, and was POSITIVE

Three of four never ran, so they hold no evidence about energy selection, and the
fourth is a positive rather than a failure to repeat. The task is the tail of an
active in-flight chain (6450 reserves the held partition, 6452 fits the objective,
6454 scores it on bytes the objective never saw) with a frozen energy and no LLM
judge or label in the ranking function. That is a forward continuation, and each
prior now carries its diagnosis and retire_if_same_verdict in the YAML.

THE DURABLE FIX IS NARROWER THAN IT LOOKED. Two manual unblocks in three hours
argue for automating this, and this milestone shows what automation must not do:
auto-override every SCOPE_MATCHED_PRIOR_FAILURE would have admitted a research
task in a settled-negative direction without anyone reading its priors. Any
planner-side fix must key on the routine-transition classes by name -- capstone,
archive-activate, terminal-handoff, plan-milestone -- and leave research tasks to
be judged.
---
 research-roadmap-next.yaml | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/research-roadmap-next.yaml b/research-roadmap-next.yaml
index cf4967172f..408629cc1e 100644
--- a/research-roadmap-next.yaml
+++ b/research-roadmap-next.yaml
@@ -329,6 +329,29 @@ tasks:
       Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
 
   - id: exp6454-held-exact-constraint-energy-selection-ab
+    prior_failures:
+    - experiment_id: exp1006-energy-selection-ssd
+      verdict: blocked_gate_check_failed
+      addressed_by: Never executed a comparison -- blocked at its own pre-gate, so it recorded no evidence
+        about energy selection. This task is gated on Exp6452's objective-causality result and runs only if
+        that lands.
+      retire_if_same_verdict: true
+    - experiment_id: exp5708-sota-exact-constraint-canary
+      verdict: 'blocked: parse_failures'
+      addressed_by: Blocked on candidate parsing, not on the selection question. This task consumes Exp6450's
+        already-parsed reserved held partition instead of re-parsing SOTA output.
+      retire_if_same_verdict: true
+    - experiment_id: exp6205-held-code-selection-v2
+      verdict: blocked_gate_check_failed
+      addressed_by: Also never ran; blocked on an upstream readiness score. Same gating class, different upstream,
+        and this task's upstream (Exp6452) is in the same milestone rather than a prior one.
+      retire_if_same_verdict: true
+    - experiment_id: exp787-sstar-energy-ranked-code-selection
+      verdict: energy_prefilter_efficient
+      addressed_by: 'The one prior that DID run, and it was POSITIVE (energy prefilter efficient), so it is
+        not a failure this task repeats. What is different: a frozen learned objective from Exp6452 and a
+        held partition the objective never saw, rather than a hand-specified prefilter on development rows.'
+      retire_if_same_verdict: true
     milestone: "2026.08.555"
     deliverable: results/experiment_6454_held_exact_constraint_energy_selection_ab.json
     title: "Gated on Exp6452 objective causality: held exact-constraint energy selection"
@@ -609,6 +632,7 @@ tasks:
       Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
 
   - id: exp6459-v555-adversarial-capstone
+    operator_override: '2026-05-29 operator directive (standing): routine milestone-transition task -- false-positive scope-match; a VN adversarial capstone scope-matches every prior capstone by construction and is structurally never a doomed rerun. This instance reconciles V555, which no prior capstone can have done.'
     milestone: "2026.08.555"
     deliverable: results/experiment_6459_v555_adversarial_capstone.json
     title: "V555 adversarial capstone and reconciliation"
